    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0852" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1247: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Trueblood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-29T19:00:00-04:32">June 29, 1931—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>63. I am reliably informed that the second Bolivian note has not yet been
                    presented but that it will be tomorrow. It is rumored that the delay was due to
                        Guachalla<anchor n="72" xml:id="d580-f1"/> having been advised by a
                    diplomatic officer of one of the neutral governments in Asuncion that the
                    Paraguayan Government would not reply to it yet. The former is understood to
                    have advised the Bolivian Foreign Office that the Paraguayan attitude was
                    reasonable and conciliatory.</p>
                <p>In view of the notice that his Government considers the incident closed, the
                    interpretation of which is still doubtful, the Paraguayan Minister has
                    officially thanked the Nuncio for his offer of mediation.</p>
                <p>The Argentine Minister saw the President yesterday and the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs today, which would seem to confirm the rumor that he has special
                    instructions.</p>
                <p>It would be appreciated if the Department would advise briefly situation in
                        Asunción.<anchor n="73" xml:id="d580-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Trueblood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d580-f1" n="72" xml:id="d580-f1-content">
                <p>Bolivian Minister in Paraguay.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d580-f2" n="73" xml:id="d580-f2-content">
                <p>The Department replied by telegram No. 26, June 30, 3 p.m.; not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
